From 2e03843816cf95d184ad4ad429adf6ea2ccc1412 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Migration Candidate <migration@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 07:22:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(runtime): isolate same-ID restore disks from live shim
 paths

A destroyed source may be restored with the same namespace and VM ID. Its captured disk filenames then overlap the recreated live shim directory. Bind that directory only at a reserved private alias, retain exact captured disk targets on tmpfs, and keep short API/vsock names through the alias cwd and standard vsock override.

Bind snapshot inputs explicitly, preserve writable log and metrics outputs, expose later shared-directory disks explicitly, and route legacy snapshot output stages to the live alias. Keep reset drive paths absolute; reuse a captured stub only after checking its entire generated slot marker and padding. Generic disk replacement remains rejected.

Extend the existing namespace probe with same-ID host-leaf preservation, dynamic disk exposure, input/output paths and host-reachable sockets. Add unit regressions for alias confinement, writable inputs and release/recapture paths. Worker namespace and VM acceptance remain required.

Signed-off-by: Migration Candidate <migration@example.invalid>
(cherry picked from commit 53d6c9b09adf8f9f1642b3c8ec6c8230b93f1c15)
